package com.specificlanguages.mops.daemon

/** Code Mode Reference entries for the `SNode` extensions: rendering, containment navigation, and indexed accessors. */
internal object CodeCatalogNodeEntries {
    val entries = listOf(
        CodeCatalog.Entry("SNode", "render", "SNode.render(): String", "extra", "Render this node with its MPS editor."),
        CodeCatalog.Entry("SNode", "descendants", "SNode.descendants: List<SNode>", "read", "Immutable snapshot of containment descendants in depth-first pre-order following native child order, excluding this node. References are not followed. Retained nodes keep native MPS validity semantics."),
        CodeCatalog.Entry("SNode", "ancestors", "SNode.ancestors: List<SNode>", "read", "Immutable snapshot of containment ancestors from parent to root, excluding this node. Retained nodes keep native MPS validity semantics."),
        CodeCatalog.Entry("SNode", "child", "SNode.child: NodeChild", "none", "Live indexed accessor. child[role] returns one SNode or null, and throws for multiple children. Assignment replaces the role with one node; null clears it. Reads require model access; writes require command access. Unknown roles fail on read and write, listing known roles. Child access uses native SNode operations; SNodeAccessUtil has no child APIs. Declared cardinality and containment constraints are not checked."),
        CodeCatalog.Entry("SNode", "children", "SNode.children: NodeChildren", "none", "Live indexed accessor. children[role] returns an immutable list of current children in order, empty for a known role without children. Assign a list to replace the role, or [] to clear. New children must be detached; existing children in the role may be retained or reordered. Reads require model access; writes require command access. Unknown roles fail on read and write, listing known roles. Child access uses native SNode operations; SNodeAccessUtil has no child APIs. Declared cardinality and containment constraints are not checked. Shadows native getChildren(), so an explicit getChildren() call returns this accessor; it iterates all children across roles in native order, so collect, findAll, each, and size() work on it. getChildren(containmentLink) remains native."),
        CodeCatalog.Entry("SNode", "references", "SNode.references: NodeReferences", "none", "Live indexed accessor. references[role] returns SReference or null; use targetNode to resolve it. Assign an SNode, SNodeReference, or SReference; null clears it. Reads require model access; writes require command access. Unknown roles fail on read and write, listing known roles. Assignments resolve the target and use SNodeAccessUtil.setReferenceTarget with MPS reference setter hooks. Unresolved targets fail without changing the reference; SReference assignments use the resolved target, not dynamic resolution information. Shadows native getReferences(), so an explicit getReferences() call returns this accessor; it iterates all set SReference values like the native collection, so collect, findAll, each, and size() work on it. getReference(referenceLink) and SNodeOperations.getReferences(node) remain native."),
        CodeCatalog.Entry("SNode", "properties", "SNode.properties: NodeProperties", "none", "Live indexed accessor: properties[name] reads with model access; properties[name] = value writes with command access. Includes inherited properties. Unset values follow MPS getter and data type defaults. Unknown properties fail on read and write, listing known ones. Assign null to request clearing through the setter. Reads and writes invoke MPS property getter/setter handlers and use persisted string values, except for enumeration properties, which read as the literal name and accept a literal name or a presentation that only one literal has; any other enumeration value fails and lists the literals. Shadows native getProperties(), so an explicit getProperties() call returns this accessor; it iterates the SProperty descriptors of set properties like the native collection. Declared descriptors are available through node.concept.properties."),
    )
}
